    "Proficiencies": "Human\nYou gain +1 in the main stat of your choice and +1 in the substat of your choice.\nYou gain +5 skill points in any non-crafting or gathering skill of your choice.\nYou can speak, read and write Common, as well as another Language of your choice. You also gain proficiency in one common weapon group.\nChosen Extra Language: Sorthen\nChosen Common Weapon Group: Small Weapons\n\nMage (Tier 1)\nRoles: Utility, Controller\nHeart: You gain +1 to Reason\nSoul: You gain +1 to either Focus or Power.\nSkills: You gain +5 skill points to spend on Appraise, Medicine, Magic, Religion, History, Flight, Artifice or Common Knowledge. You can exchange any skill point for 2 expertise points, but must spend them in these skills.\nKey Ability: Mage's Journey\n\nElementalist (Tier 2)\nRoles: Striker, Controller\nHeart: You gain +1 to Reason or Presence.\nSoul: You gain +1 to Focus or Agility.\nSkills: You gain +5 skill points to spend on Magic, Artifice, Perception, Linguistics or Common Knowledge. You can exchange any skill point for 2 expertise points, but must spend them in these skills.\nKey Ability: Elemental Convergence\n\nResolved Class Benefits\nMage: +1 Focus from Soul.\nMage class: Magic +5 skill",
    "Items": "Starting Funds\nBase Clim: 3000\nBreakthrough Bonus: 0\nEquipment Cost: 1350\nRemaining Clim: 2650\n\nArmor (Clothing)\nEquipment | Armor | 500 Clim | 0\nA high quality set of clothing. Does not provide any bonuses by itself, but if crafted by an armorsmith, can accept Flamellon mods.\nCannot be worn at the same time as regular armor.\nMods:\nA modsMage Robes (20 points): You gain +1 maximum mana, but lose 1 guard and 2 block.\n\nB modsCloud Robes (50 points): Your movement speed is increased by 5ft.\nBattle Casting (80 points): The first spell you cast each turn does not provoke attacks of opportunity.\n\nFrame modsReinforced Clothing (0 points): This clothing can benefit from material bonuses, but its burden is increased by 1.\n\nWand (One-Handed)\nEquipment | Channeling Weapon | 500 Clim | 1\nMagic Blast: You may alter the damage type fired by an attack made with this weapon for 0 AP. The damage type must be an element type you have mastered (usually unlocked through classes) or one that’s built into the weapon. Each weapon has at least one element built in.\nRange: 60ft\nMods\nA mods:Ornamental (10 points): You may use this weapon as one minor item such as an instrument or parasol.\nEcho Blast (20 points): When you make a basic Heavy attack, you may split the damage against two different targets in range. Make only 1 accuracy check against both.\nWarding Wand (35 points): You may spend 1 AP to gain 5 temporary HP until the start of your next turn.\n\nB mods:Dedicated Focus (50 points): Gain +1 bonus to accuracy rolls, but can only fire elemental attacks of 1 element. Spells cast through this wand only gain that bonus if they deal that element of damage.\nMana Core (80 points): When you deal max damage with an attack made with this weapon or with a spell cast through this weapon against an enemy in an encounter, your next spell this turn costs 1 less mana (min 0)\n\nResearch Kit\nAdventuring Essentials | Kit | 100 Clim | 1\nHas enough bottles/vials/containers to store research samples for one expedition.\nThe kit is consumed at the end of the expedition if used.\n\nAdventurer's Kit\nAdventuring Essentials | Kit | 100 Clim | 1\nAdventuring kits contain all of the basic tools for adventuring. Included in the kit: Backpack, Flint and steel, Rope, Notebook, Pen, Compass, Bedroll, Torches, Hand Mirror.\nEffect: You can use the items for their various purposes within reason. Can store up to 5 burden of Adventuring Essentials, a Northi Lantern or items included in this kit in a combat ready state for 0 burden and contains a torch/lantern holster for hands off torch/lantern use for light purposes. Cannot store kits or other burden reducing items in this combat ready state.\n\nHealing Potion\nAlchemy | Potion | 150 Clim | 1\nHealing liquid in a vial made from various herbs and reagents. Spurs the body’s natural healing by converting mana into regeneration. When drank, you heal 15 HP.\nCrafting:\nMaterials: 450 Alchemy Materials\nHerbs: None required",
